topics,list_help,lh,help
Help is available on the following topics.  Type "help <topic>".
   commands   overview   moving     objects    fighting   magic
   sorcerer   multip     modes      abbrev     save       multics
   news       info
For a one-line list of every command, type "commands".
end;
commands,command
Movement : north(n) south(s) east(e) west(w) up(u) down(d) in out jump
Objects  : get drop throw eat plug wave(swing) read look what
Info     : commands help info news score turns modes list_help(lh)
Game     : save restore send quit(stop,end) brief fast full on off
Comms    : talk (multiplayer)
Special  : multics(m,..) cross sorcerer abbrev(ab) set_modes(stm)
Type "help <topic>" for more detail on a group.
end;
overview
Explore is a cave-exploration adventure.  You move from room to room
with one-word commands, collecting treasures and avoiding (or killing)
the creatures that live in the cave.  Score points by carrying
treasures back out to the surface and by defeating creatures.  A
perfect game earns the rank of Grand Master Explorer.  Type "commands"
for the full list, "help moving" to get started, and "news" for recent
changes.
end;
moving,move,n,north,s,south,e,east,w,west,u,up,d,down,in,out,jump,go
Move with a single direction word: north, south, east, west, up, down
(or just n, s, e, w, u, d).  "in" and "out" work at the shack.  In some
rooms you may also type the name of an adjacent room to go there.
"jump" jumps.  "look" reprints the full room description.  The "brief",
"full", and "fast" modes control how much room description you see on
each visit (say "help modes").  You need a light to see in dark rooms.
end;
objects,object,get,drop,throw,eat,plug,wave,swing,read,look,what
"get <thing>" picks an object up; "drop <thing>" sets it down; "get
all" and "drop all" work too.  "throw <thing>" hurls it, "eat <thing>"
tries to eat it, "read <thing>" reads it, and "wave" (or "swing")
waves what you are holding.  "what" lists what you are carrying.
"plug" plugs a device into a receptacle.  Carry treasures back to the
shack and "drop" them there to score.
end;
fighting,fight,kill,attack
Creatures block your way and can kill you.  Each creature has a
particular weapon that defeats it -- the wrong one just annoys it, so
experiment and pay attention to what you find near each creature.
"throw" the correct object at a creature to defeat it.  A knife works
on the wandering dwarves that throw knives at you.  If you are killed,
the sorcerer may reincarnate you.
end;
magic,word,words
Certain words spoken in the right rooms have surprising effects, such
as transporting you elsewhere.  Watch for hints carved on walls and
written on notes -- and remember the magic words you learn.  Some words
are just a familiar idea read backwards.
end;
sorcerer
The cave has a sorcerer who moves through it and can speak to
explorers, send them messages, and reincarnate the dead.  Knowing the
sorcerer's secret word lets a player enter sorcerer mode with the
"sorcerer" command.  In multiplayer mode the sorcerer can see and
reach the other players.
end;
multip,multiplayer,talk
Explore can be played by several people at once, sharing one cave.
This is off by default; type "multip" to turn it on (or put "multip"
in your start_up.explore to enable it every game).  With multip on,
other players and the sorcerer can see you, and you can message another
player in your room with "talk".  Type "^multip" to turn it back off.
Multiplayer must also be permitted by the installation and you must
have access to the shared files; if not, "multip" reports that it is
unavailable.  The objects and creatures are still private to your own
game -- multiplayer only adds mutual visibility and messaging.
end;
modes,mode,set_modes,stm,st,brief,full,fast,quit,on,off
"modes" shows your current settings.  Three control how much room
description you see:
   full   always print the long description (the default)
   brief  long description the first time you enter a room, short
          description on later visits
   fast   always print the short description
"quit"/"^quit" control the break (interrupt) key:
   quit   the break key works normally (the default)
   ^quit  the break key is disabled, so you cannot accidentally
          break out of the game -- you leave only with "quit"
"multip"/"^multip" turn multiplayer on and off.  "set_modes" (or
"stm") sets several at once, e.g.  stm brief,^quit,multip
end;
abbrev,ab,.a,.ab,.d,.l,.la,.ls,.lx,.e,.p,.s,.u,.q
"abbrev" (or "ab") begins using abbrevs -- your own shorthand for
commands.  Sub-commands:
   .a   add an abbrev
   .ab  add an abbrev expanded only at the start of a line
   .d   delete an abbrev
   .l   list abbrevs          .la  list those beginning with a character
   .ls  list those containing a string
   .lx  list those whose expansion contains a string
   .e   edit abbrevs (.e all, or .e last for the last expansion)
   .p   print the abbrev segment pathname
   .s   print the expansion of a line
   .u   use another abbrev segment
   .q   stop using abbrevs
end;
save,restore
"save [name]" writes your game to a file (default SAVED_GAME_) so you
can continue later; "restore [name]" reads it back.  Saved games are
kept in your home directory.  The cave must be open to restore.
end;
multics,m,..
"multics <command>" (or "m <command>", or "..<command>") runs a Multics
command without leaving the game -- handy for checking your working
directory, listing a segment, and the like.  For example, "..pwd"
prints your working directory and returns you to the game.
end;
score,turns,send,cross
"score" shows your current points; "turns" shows how many moves you
have made.  "send" leaves a message on the rock for the next explorer.
"cross" attempts to cross an obstacle when you are suitably equipped.
end;
quit,stop,end
"quit" (also "stop" or "end") leaves the game.  You are asked to
confirm.  Save your game first with "save" if you want to continue
later -- quitting does not save automatically.
end;
news
"news" prints recent changes and notes about this version of the game.
end;
info
"info" prints background information about Explore and the facilities
available to explorers, including saving, restoring, and getting help.
Outside the game, "help explore" gives a reference overview.
end;
